Z||000011||CityChick||03-13-2001||05:40 AM||||I think you guys handled the last thread about creationism wisely, by ending it.  I'm always getting into arguments about christians and non-christians, but starting up another thread about the same ordeal after pleasantly ended the one prior?  I hate to say that some of the things are slightly offensive that are being said, I'm never one to speak out about things, but have a little respect for the subject, it may not be the most wonderful thing to get into, but you have to respect eachother, and other persons ideas.  I've read through the other thread never commenting, because I didn't want to get into it, but I realized that I had respect for each of the people commenting.  You were showing your views, and defending yourselces, sometimes out of spite, and sometimes to try to prove a point.  <BR>I'm a young christian, and it's hard living the life that i've lived, being persecuted by christians for not being "a good enough christian", and still retaining the faith I have in God.  I dislike the christians that tell other people that "You are going to burn in hell if you don't accept Jesus Christ as your personal saviour." That's just not right and they make the non-believers generalize christians.  I for one hate to be hated, and I never want to come off as a christian that would be cruel to another human being.  Christians are not here to judge, that's God's almighty right, to have the final say in who goes to heaven or hell.  Christians should only help spread the word of the gospel, and if it is unwelcome then pray that it will be spread in it's own way and time.  <BR>Badgering will get you nowhere, and these threads will get you nowhere either.  I was intrigued by them I have to say, but now they're bringing up more bad than good. About the mass killings that christians did, why god allows such pain and death, and why we have to be mortal at all, I believe that life is a test.  We were made perfect, in god's image, but Adam ate the apple and god showed him all the pains of the world, which he was protected from before.  So now Heaven must be earned.  This is just my theory, and I understand how It could sound like a fairy tale.  I believe souls are what seperate us from the animals, and I'm sorry, but souls cannot evolve.  At least not in my world.  I'm only a freshman in college and haven't been as experienced in the world as many of you in the forum who have been steadily occupied in posting about this topic, but I believe I know my faith. Please do not try to insult me about my youth or my misunderstanding of anything I have said.  <BR>I hope all of this will just end and you can go back to talking about what you all have in common and love: your fieros.  I'm going to end saying that I believe everyone has wonderful characteristics, no matter what they believe in, and what you believe doesn't make you a bad person, but uniquely wonderful.  I have never judged anyone as a christian, and hope never to do so.  So i hope this christianity thing ends soon, and please, don't be too offensive, remember there are some people that could be hurt with your actions whenever you realize it or not.  ||||reg||1
